    ipbes:hasDescription "Habitat maintenance, pollination (established but incomplete), regulation of freshwater quantity and quality, formation and protection of soils and regulation of floods are declining because of land-use intensification designed to increase the production of crops, livestock, aquaculture, forest biomass and cotton, as well as urban development (well established) {2.2.1, 2.2.2, 2.2.5}. Trade-offs between material and regulating contributions have compromised food and water security in some areas {2.2.1, 2.2.2, 2.2.5}." ;
    dcterms:identifier "2.2.1, 2.2.2, 2.2.5" .

<http://ontology.ipbes.net/report/subm/ECA18-A2-SM3> a ipbes:SubMessage ;
